  "sandbox": "Ledger, receipts and both STOP files live in tasks/, STOP-owner and STOP-agentic inside --workdir (tasks.root() checked to be inside it); only AlcorSystem tasks.py is imported; no process control, no systemd, no live worker or home-directory state is used; the only network is loopback to the effect receiver; the suite starts no processes of its own except one git rev-parse.",
  "limitations": "A finite suite shows no more than the trials it ran: trials per family are small and the faults are injected at fixed points, not found by chance. Real-seam families (before-reservation, worker-exit-before-dispatch, stale-lease-generation, stop-while-pending) exercise tasks.py create/renew/sweep/close in a sandbox ledger; all other families (after-reservation, ack-lost, duplicate-delivery, provider-timeout, out-of-order-receipt, receipt-source-mismatch) are simulated in the suite. tasks.py has no worker-generation fence, so the old worker's late effect is withheld by the suite after the real ledger refuses its tasks.renew on the ABANDONED task; no receiver-side generation fence is tested. The fake receiver is a loopback stand-in, not a real provider. Finished real tasks are not marked DONE (the DONE audit needs verified evidence the sandbox does not model); a sweep after the run abandons their lapsed leases. STOP trials are reported as quarantined, never recovered, although the matrix lists stop-while-pending as retry_safe, so the retry-safe recovery rates (overall and real-seam) are lowered by those trials: quote them with the STOP family's 0 expected effects in mind. The duplicate-delivery guard is an in-run, in-memory set. Recovery times for lease families include the lease wait. Retry-safe recovery rates should be quoted from the real-seam cohort or with the simulated share stated.",
